"2eeh50c0gnl": "Ten Days at Haselöd",
"18ro0wst7pg": "Oberröding, Kelbach district, Bavaria (fictional)",
"21166lq824t": "Inspired by the Hinterkaifeck murders (1922, Bavaria)",
"27ltrko0gu3": "About 35 min",
"24lliu4umoh": "The examination findings and inspection records in this file describe in detail the wounds of four people killed by repeated blows to the head with a farm tool, and the blood and drag marks frozen onto a barn floor. The file also contains bloodstained scene photographs.",
"1x57sv15p08": "Winter 1923. A lonely farm across snow-covered fields. Ten days from the last sighting to the discovery.",
"1799uvq8brx": "**Evidence File 02** · Tgb.-Nr. 41/1923 · Gendarmerie-Station Oberröding · transferred to Kelbach District Office",
"em7zrc72vj": "A work of fiction that borrows only the motif of the 1922 murders at a remote Bavarian farm. The villages, farm, people and institutions are all invented and bear no relation to real persons.",
"15xayom5bad": "A bundle of papers handed over by the Kelbach District Office. Choose a file from the tabs at the top, then take the papers out one at a time from the list on the left.",
"233rgb36qqd": "Case Summary — Unnatural Deaths",
"16th3cz7s7f": "Found",
"1akocykvi9w": "Afternoon of Monday, February 5, 1923 · the isolated [[Haselöd farm|k_haselod]], half an hour across the fields from [[Oberröding|k_oberroding]]",
"15vmb91bb2f": "Deceased",
"nnhb31yyqh": "Farmer [[Michael Moosbauer|k_michael]] (71) · wife [[Walburga Moosbauer|k_walburga]] (68) · daughter [[Rosa Moosbauer|k_rosa]] (37) · maid [[Thekla Haider|k_thekla]] (54)",
"1jmp89sip8k": "Cause of death",
"x4cymg7fjb": "All four: head injuries from repeated blows — apparently a farm tool with a hammer face on one side and a blade on the other (opinion of the Kelbach district physician)",
